# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS - never commit these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local database credentials.
.env

# Streamlit's real secrets file, which will hold your Neon connection string.
# The .example version IS committed, so others know what to fill in.
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENVIRONMENT - big, machine-specific, and rebuildable from requirements.txt
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA - regenerated by running the pipeline.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The raw download (src/load_data.py fetches it) and the processed CSV
# (src/features.py rebuilds it). No reason to store either in git; the code
# that produces them is the real artifact.
data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODELS - deliberately COMMITTED. Read on.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The usual advice is "never commit binaries to git", and usually it's right.
# We commit these anyway, on purpose:
#
#   1. The deployed dashboard needs them. Streamlit Cloud clones this repo and
#      runs app/dashboard.py -- it does not train anything. No model in the
#      repo means no working demo.
#   2. They're small. xgboost.joblib is ~360KB. The rule exists to stop people
#      committing 2GB checkpoints, and it doesn't apply at this size.
#   3. They're what makes the results reproducible for a reader who just wants
#      to check your numbers without running the pipeline.
#
# If these ever grow past a few MB, the right answer is Git LFS or a model
# registry -- not a .gitignore line that silently breaks the deployment.
#
# outputs/models/*.joblib is intentionally NOT ignored.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / EDITOR noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
